Given this Wage interface:

```
public interface Wage {
    default void notice() {
        System.out.println("Executing ...");
    }
    void increase();
}
```

Given this Employee class:

```
public class Employee implements Wage {
    private String id;
    private String name;
    private int salary;
```

```
    public Employee(String id, String name) {
        this.id = id;
        this.name = name;
        this.salary = 1000;
    }
```

```
    @Override
    public void notice() {
        System.out.println("Employee salary computed!");
    }
```

```
    @Override
    public void increase() {
        this.salary += 200;
    }
```

```
    public int getSalary() {
        return salary;
    }
}
```

and this main method:

```
public static void main(String[] args) {
    Employee e = new Employee("EMP101", "John Doe");
    try {
        e.increase();
        System.out.println("Salary: " + e.getSalary());
}
catch (Exception ex) {
        System.out.println("Cannot increase/decrease salary.");
}
finally {
        e.notice();
    }
}
```

What will be printed on the screen after running the main method?

